From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@local>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keep relocation metadata outside the flat image

C++ static libraries produce retained MIPS relocation sections large enough
for GNU ld to reject elf2flt.ld's historical overlapping `.junk 0` output
section.  The section is only ELF metadata consumed by elf2flt and must not
be allocated into the bFLT data image.  Give it the GNU ld INFO type: this
retains the relocations without assigning SHF_ALLOC or a load address.
---
 elf2flt.ld.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/elf2flt.ld.in b/elf2flt.ld.in
index 1fed6d8..c8c9ac1 100644
--- a/elf2flt.ld.in
+++ b/elf2flt.ld.in
@@ -230 +230 @@
-	.junk 0 : { *(.rel*) *(.rela*) }
+	.junk 0 (INFO) : { *(.rel*) *(.rela*) }
-- 
